Summary of Missing/Superfluous Fields

Add:

ipniId: Ask Gemini to find the IPNI ID (e.g., "12653-1"). This allows you to build a link: https://www.ipni.org/a/${ipniId}.

standardAbbreviation: You have abbreviation, but ensure the prompt specifically asks for the standard form used in citations.

Remove:

patrons: Usually irrelevant for 20th/21st-century botanists and prone to hallucinations for 18th-century ones (confused with employers).

cityOfBirth / cityOfDeath: Combine these into birthPlace and deathPlace. The granularity of "City" sometimes causes the model to hallucinate a city when only the country is known.

Prompt Engineering Tweak for "Eponymous Taxa"

To strictly kill hallucinations on taxa, change the description in your botanistProfileSchema:

code
TypeScript
download
content_copy
expand_less
eponymousTaxa: { 
  type: Type.ARRAY, 
  description: 'List validly published taxa. YOU MUST INCLUDE THE YEAR OF PUBLICATION IN THE NAME string if possible to prove verification. Example: "Banksia L.f. (1782)". If you cannot find a specific year, do not include it.',
  // ...
}

Asking for the Year acts as a "cognitive speedbump" for the LLM; it's much harder to hallucinate a correct year alongside a fake name than just a fake name alone.

